### Questions

**Q1.** What is the main purpose of Requirement Engineering?

A) To write code
B) To find out and define what the software should do
C) To design the database
D) To test the final software

---

**Q2.** A customer says:

> "I want an online shopping system."

The development team talks to the customer, asks questions, and gathers detailed requirements.

Which RE activity is this?

A) Validation
B) Elicitation
C) Management
D) Implementation

---

**Q3.** The team has collected 50 requirements. They now check whether the requirements are **consistent, complete, feasible, and unambiguous**.

Which activity is this?

A) Elicitation
B) Analysis
C) Coding
D) Deployment

---

**Q4.** The team writes the agreed requirements in a formal document.

What is this document called?

A) Design Document
B) Test Plan
C) SRS
D) User Manual

---

**Q5.** Which of these is a **functional requirement**?

A) The system should respond within 2 seconds.
B) The system should be available 99.9% of the time.
C) The user should be able to reset their password.
D) The system should be secure.

---

**Q6.** Which is a **non-functional requirement**?

A) User can add products to cart.
B) User can cancel an order.
C) User can create an account.
D) The system should support 10,000 simultaneous users.

---

**Q7.** After the SRS has been prepared, the customer discovers:

> "We actually need an option to pay using UPI."

Which RE activity deals with handling this **change in requirements**?

A) Requirement Management
B) Requirement Elicitation
C) Coding
D) Deployment

